MiniMax-H3 video engine (h3), vendored

Source: the h3 engine repository, branch native, commit
222d8c3 (after "Synthetic-weights mode" and the native prep, audio VAE and
mp4 writer), on top of main 8c4a054. Plain copy, without its git history, by dev/tools/vendor_video.sh.

What came from where:

  h3 runtime/{engine,media,model,ops}/*  -> runtime/video/{engine,media,model,ops}/
  h3 runtime/metal/MetalBackend.*        -> runtime/video/metal/
  h3 include/h3/h3.h (C ABI)             -> runtime/video/abi/h3.h
  h3 runtime/metal/abi/*                 -> runtime/metal/abi/video/
  h3 runtime/metal/kernels/common/*      -> runtime/metal/kernels/video/common/
  h3 runtime/metal/kernels/GROUP/F       -> runtime/metal/kernels/video/GROUP_F
                                            (GROUP: dit, vae, audio, prep, preview;
                                            shared/F -> F)
  h3 tools/convert_*.py, h3/{common,config,safetensors}.py
                                         -> install/video (install/video/VENDORED)

The include paths are rewritten for these locations ("engine/" ->
"video/engine/" and likewise for media, model and ops,
"metal/MetalBackend.hpp" -> "video/metal/MetalBackend.hpp", "metal/abi/" ->
"metal/abi/video/", "metal/kernels/common/" -> "metal/kernels/video/common/",
"h3/h3.h" -> "video/abi/h3.h"). Code and kernel arithmetic are unchanged but
for one local patch, which the script reapplies and which belongs upstream:
WeightStream.mm creates each slot's `free` semaphore at 0 and signals it once
instead of creating it at 1. libdispatch traps (SIGTRAP, "Semaphore object
deallocated while in use") when a semaphore is disposed below its creation
value, which a slot the SSD reader holds is when a streamed DiT is released.

Splash's own files beside the vendored tree: VideoJob.{hpp,mm} (the
`splash video-native` process the server runs per job) and this note.

Build: the kernels compile with Splash's production Metal flags into
splash.metallib (the video kernel group); the request preparation's kernels
(prep_*.metal) also without fast math, as h3 compiles them, since they
reproduce MLX's arithmetic bit for bit. The host code compiles with Splash's
flags plus -ffp-contract=off, as h3 builds it, into
build/engine/libsplash-video.a; the mp4 writer links AVFoundation, CoreMedia
and CoreVideo. With main 8c4a054 vendored this way, the 3 s golden request's
final latents, video VAE frames and TAEH3 preview frames were byte-identical
to h3's references (make test-video-real); the synthetic-weight forward
(dev/tests/engine/video_synthetic_metal_test.mm) checks the DiT kernels
without weight files.

